# The square tour: 600 mm sides, CCW, axis-aligned -- four legs driven
# straight through, four 90 deg pivots.
#
# AXIS-ALIGNED means each leg runs along one axis of the tour's own
# start frame: leg 1 all +x, leg 2 all +y, and so on. Until 2026-09-01
# the chart drew it as a DIAMOND, because the plot was in the robot's
# raw odometry frame; run_tour.py now always charts in the start frame.
# For a figure that is genuinely turned 45 deg, see diamond.tour.
#
# SIZING. 600 mm sides span 600 x 600 mm; the usable field is
# +-600 x +-400 mm and the working budget +-550 x +-350 (tours/FIELD.md),
# so 600 is the largest round side that fits the tight (y) axis.
# Stage the robot at (-300, -300) facing East to sit centred -- driven
# from the field CENTRE this square reaches +600 mm and does not fit.
#
# PIVOT SPEED. omega=180 deg/s (~188 mm/s at the wheel), not the
# 45 deg/s this file was ported with: MEASURED gopiv 2026-09-01, 45 deg/s
# is 47 mm/s at the wheel, at the stiction floor -- pivots took 4.5-5.0 s
# and chattered between 0 and 75 mm/s while the straights held a clean
# 144 mm/s. 188 mm/s also measured MORE accurate than 300 (excess
# +1.34 deg sd 0.35 vs +6.88 sd 1.03, n=8 each, interleaved A/B).
#
# NO SET BLOCK, NO MID-LEG STOPS (removed 2026-09-06). Until then this
# file carried `SET speed_floor/yaw_taper/pivot_overrun` -- all RETIRED
# ordinals after the config consolidation, answered `err` and silently
# no-ops -- plus `SET twist_hold_gain 8`, a retune field_dance.py had
# already dropped as harmful on this engine. It also split legs 1 and 3
# with a `STOP dwell=0.6`: that was radio-robot-elite's test fixture for
# ITS planned-`STOP` wire verb ("the umbrella issue's two stops on
# opposite legs"), ported verbatim; here STOP is a host-side sleep and
# every TWIST is already its own MOVE_X, so the split tested nothing and
# added two accel/decel cycles per lap. A tour is a benchmark of the
# firmware's defaults; it must not retune the robot.
#
# MEASURED tovez 2026-09-06, bench, pure odometry, firmware 1.20260906.6
# (reports/square-hw-vs-sim-20260906/bench-demo/square_clean-floorcredit.json):
# closure 11.0 mm at the baked lag 0.13. Same tour, same bench, on the
# full-coast-credit arrival predicate an hour earlier: 387.4 mm.
# Reference: gopiv 2026-09-01, pre-029 engine, 5.0 mm
# (reports/tours-20260901.md).

MARK leg1
TWIST vx=250 dist=600 timeout=8
TWIST omega=180 angle=90 timeout=6

MARK leg2
TWIST vx=250 dist=600 timeout=8
TWIST omega=180 angle=90 timeout=6

MARK leg3
TWIST vx=250 dist=600 timeout=8
TWIST omega=180 angle=90 timeout=6

MARK leg4
TWIST vx=250 dist=600 timeout=8
TWIST omega=180 angle=90 timeout=6
STOP dwell=0.5
